1
00:00:01,181 --> 00:00:09,221
The Princess Sapphire
Knight of the Ribbon

2
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:50,160
♪ Atashi no miru yume himitsu nano ♪
The dreams I see are my secret

3
00:00:51,250 --> 00:00:57,089
♪ Dare ni mo iwanai himitsu nano ♪
I won’t tell anyone—it’s my secret

4
00:00:58,541 --> 00:01:02,461
♪ Akai manto hira hira ♪
A red cape fluttering

5
00:01:02,462 --> 00:01:04,981
♪ Uma o tobasu oujo ♪
Galloping on a horse—the princess

6
00:01:04,981 --> 00:01:06,901
♪ Sore ga atashi ♪
That’s me!

7
00:01:07,621 --> 00:01:10,901
♪ Lula-dula-lula-dula ♪
-

8
00:01:10,905 --> 00:01:13,424
♪ Lulu laa, lulaa ♪
-

9
00:01:14,541 --> 00:01:18,021
♪ Lula-dula-lula-dula ♪
-

10
00:01:18,140 --> 00:01:20,741
♪ Lulu laa, lulaa ♪
-

11
00:01:21,500 --> 00:01:25,220
♪ Ribon no kishi wa ♪
The Knight of the Ribbon,

12
00:01:25,220 --> 00:01:28,621
♪ Honto wa hontto wa ♪
Truly, truly,

13
00:01:28,622 --> 00:01:31,822
♪ Atashi nano sa ♪
It’s really me!

14
00:01:44,101 --> 00:01:50,141
Thirteenth Episode
The Castle of Roses
Rose House

15
00:02:02,373 --> 00:02:04,080
I'm bored already.

16
00:02:06,724 --> 00:02:08,340
Isn't there anything fun to do?

17
00:02:09,990 --> 00:02:12,140
Prince Sapphire, it is time.

18
00:02:12,265 --> 00:02:16,593
The closing ceremony is set for 10 o'clock! Why are you dawdling?

19
00:02:17,585 --> 00:02:20,160
It's time, Prince Sapphire.

20
00:02:23,270 --> 00:02:24,320
Take that!

21
00:02:24,340 --> 00:02:26,540
Is it time for the ceremony...?

22
00:02:27,300 --> 00:02:28,300
Head!

23
00:02:28,500 --> 00:02:29,500
You two!

24
00:02:31,380 --> 00:02:32,380
Head!

25
00:02:32,640 --> 00:02:33,640
Chest!

26
00:02:34,780 --> 00:02:35,300
Head!

27
00:02:35,800 --> 00:02:36,800
Right!

28
00:02:42,670 --> 00:02:43,820
Now's your chance, run!

29
00:02:44,870 --> 00:02:46,143
Prince Sapphire!

30
00:02:56,700 --> 00:02:58,680
Well now, Your Highness, where are you off to?

31
00:02:59,410 --> 00:03:00,820
Where I go is none of your business.

32
00:03:00,844 --> 00:03:05,160
Forgive my intrusion, but please do not go to the Southern Valley.

33
00:03:05,344 --> 00:03:06,344
The Southern Valley?

34
00:03:06,700 --> 00:03:08,900
It is quite dangerous, with frequent rockslides.

35
00:03:09,320 --> 00:03:10,320
Good to know!

36
00:03:11,640 --> 00:03:13,560
He’s headed for the Southern Valley, Nylon!

37
00:03:13,780 --> 00:03:14,339
Yes!

38
00:03:22,780 --> 00:03:26,899
The Southern Valley, huh... Dangerous with frequent rockslides sounds like fun!

39
00:03:27,086 --> 00:03:28,200
Hyah!

40
00:03:32,780 --> 00:03:34,340
Who could have thrown this away?

41
00:03:39,280 --> 00:03:41,300
There isn't even a rockslide.

42
00:03:41,704 --> 00:03:42,920
That Duke Duralumin...

43
00:03:43,475 --> 00:03:44,740
Why would he say such a thing?

44
00:03:51,810 --> 00:03:53,866
Dejira in the Southern Valley is still there too.

45
00:03:56,400 --> 00:03:57,533
Hyah!

46
00:04:07,080 --> 00:04:09,286
The camouflage curtain is peeling right off!

47
00:04:09,600 --> 00:04:10,395
You idiot!

48
00:04:10,420 --> 00:04:11,060
Forgive me!

49
00:04:11,320 --> 00:04:11,800
Turn it!

50
00:04:19,810 --> 00:04:21,959
Phew, good thing they didn't find me.

51
00:04:25,440 --> 00:04:27,240
The flowers are as lovely as ever.

52
00:04:29,040 --> 00:04:30,200
What's wrong, Opal?

53
00:04:36,600 --> 00:04:38,653
What is it, Opal?

54
00:04:42,945 --> 00:04:44,800
Hey, Opal, what's gotten into you?

55
00:04:44,980 --> 00:04:46,540
It's just an old ruin! What a letdown!

56
00:05:07,286 --> 00:05:08,600
Who are you?

57
00:05:08,870 --> 00:05:10,380
You are Master Sapphire, aren't you?

58
00:05:10,910 --> 00:05:12,340
That's right—Prince Sapphire.

59
00:05:13,165 --> 00:05:14,165
A prince?

60
00:05:14,770 --> 00:05:15,880
That's right, the Prince.

61
00:05:16,205 --> 00:05:17,205
Who are you?

62
00:05:21,480 --> 00:05:23,780
We shall meet again, Master Sapphire.

63
00:05:25,980 --> 00:05:26,980
Call me Prince!

64
00:05:27,270 --> 00:05:28,270
And tell me your name!

65
00:05:37,490 --> 00:05:39,380
A strange perfume scent...

66
00:06:00,890 --> 00:06:02,180
Who's there?

67
00:06:12,000 --> 00:06:13,000
Halt!

68
00:06:34,738 --> 00:06:35,446
Who goes there?

69
00:06:39,235 --> 00:06:41,980
We have come from the House of Roses to escort you.

70
00:06:43,070 --> 00:06:44,070
The House of Roses?

71
00:07:01,140 --> 00:07:02,700
That's that strange perfume!

72
00:07:23,145 --> 00:07:23,960
The House of Roses?

73
00:07:38,190 --> 00:07:40,960
Was there always a place like this in the Southern Valley?

74
00:07:57,573 --> 00:07:59,280
This is the Rose Mansion.

75
00:08:09,890 --> 00:08:11,020
Rose perfume!

76
00:08:56,959 --> 00:08:58,243
Sapphire,...

77
00:08:59,561 --> 00:09:01,960
please head to the white rose boat on the right.

78
00:09:47,300 --> 00:09:48,640
Sapphire... Welcome, Master Sapphire.

79
00:09:49,206 --> 00:09:50,740
So it really was you.

80
00:09:51,215 --> 00:09:52,860
My name is Duke Blanc.

81
00:09:53,200 --> 00:09:54,200
Duke Blanc?

82
00:09:54,530 --> 00:09:55,530
Why did you call for me?

83
00:09:55,920 --> 00:09:56,920
Yes, Master Sapphire.

84
00:09:57,740 --> 00:10:03,580
How many thousands of years has it been since our ancestors first settled in this corner of Silverland?

85
00:10:04,859 --> 00:10:08,340
We take pride in being born here and in dying here.

86
00:10:09,442 --> 00:10:14,080
But lately, someone has been trying to drive us from this land.

87
00:10:14,962 --> 00:10:16,964
Prince Sapphire, please help me!

88
00:10:18,095 --> 00:10:19,920
We can only live in this land.

89
00:10:20,820 --> 00:10:23,860
Duke Blanc, who on earth is trying to drive you away?

90
00:10:24,740 --> 00:10:25,800
It's Grand Duke Duralumin.

91
00:10:26,260 --> 00:10:27,260
Duralumin?

92
00:10:27,360 --> 00:10:29,641
Promise me you'll help! Yes!

93
00:10:31,799 --> 00:10:33,100
That Duralumin...

94
00:10:33,960 --> 00:10:34,280
All right!

95
00:10:34,560 --> 00:10:35,560
I promise!

96
00:10:44,949 --> 00:10:47,540
What good is Prince Sapphire going to be?!

97
00:10:48,139 --> 00:10:49,640
Duke Rouge, how insolent!

98
00:10:50,350 --> 00:10:51,680
Please forgive my brother's rudeness.

99
00:10:52,760 --> 00:10:53,760
Brother?

100
00:10:53,944 --> 00:10:56,793
I am sick and tired of this weed-infested land!

101
00:10:57,360 --> 00:11:00,340
Why don't we just hand it over to Grand Duke Duralumin?!

102
00:11:00,789 --> 00:11:02,000
What are you saying, you shameless fool?!

103
00:11:02,560 --> 00:11:04,117
Are you planning to betray me and our comrades?!

104
00:11:04,380 --> 00:11:05,380
Say whatever you like.

105
00:11:05,740 --> 00:11:06,740
My mind is made up.

106
00:11:07,080 --> 00:11:08,580
We'll just get other land in return.

107
00:11:09,285 --> 00:11:11,780
This is a magnificent land fit for a king, without a single weed in sight!

108
00:11:12,840 --> 00:11:13,220
Rouge!

109
00:11:13,640 --> 00:11:14,640
Let's do this!

110
00:11:14,960 --> 00:11:15,340
Wait!

111
00:11:15,680 --> 00:11:16,826
Stop this! You're brothers!

112
00:11:16,900 --> 00:11:17,900
Prince Sapphire!

113
00:11:18,050 --> 00:11:19,460
You'd best stay out of this for your own good.

114
00:11:20,000 --> 00:11:21,500
For the sake of your secret, too!

115
00:11:22,680 --> 00:11:23,680
A secret?

116
00:11:23,980 --> 00:11:24,400
Rouge!

117
00:11:24,789 --> 00:11:26,500
Exploiting someone's secret is cowardly!

118
00:11:26,501 --> 00:11:27,560
Like I care!

119
00:11:27,930 --> 00:11:30,180
Even my brother knows the Prince's secret.

120
00:11:30,500 --> 00:11:33,660
We brothers have a knack for seeing right through people's secrets.

121
00:11:34,180 --> 00:11:35,580
What do the two of you claim to know?!

122
00:11:35,840 --> 00:11:36,440
Sapphire!

123
00:11:36,745 --> 00:11:37,880
You are a woman!

124
00:11:40,660 --> 00:11:41,040
Rouge!

125
00:11:41,520 --> 00:11:44,540
Brother or not, I cannot forgive your cowardly ways!

126
00:11:44,880 --> 00:11:45,880
Draw your sword!

127
00:12:02,029 --> 00:12:03,060
Now you've done it, Sapphire!

128
00:12:04,840 --> 00:12:05,940
I told you to stop!

129
00:12:06,680 --> 00:12:07,500
Why should I listen to you?

130
00:12:07,690 --> 00:12:08,690
Master Sapphire!

131
00:12:08,740 --> 00:12:09,260
Watch out!

132
00:12:09,600 --> 00:12:10,495
Kumambagio!

133
00:12:10,520 --> 00:12:11,871
Sapphire, take that!

134
00:12:14,500 --> 00:12:15,500
My Master Sapphire!

135
00:12:15,700 --> 00:12:16,700
Run! Get away!

136
00:12:31,320 --> 00:12:32,473
Master Sapphire!

137
00:12:34,500 --> 00:12:35,500
Master Sapphire!

138
00:12:38,840 --> 00:12:39,840
Master Sapphire!

139
00:13:10,709 --> 00:13:12,060
What a strange night that was.

140
00:13:12,479 --> 00:13:13,980
Please protect our land.

141
00:13:56,550 --> 00:13:58,040
It's a magnificent fortress.

142
00:13:58,260 --> 00:14:00,393
Once the cliffside artillery is complete,

143
00:14:00,417 --> 00:14:03,280
crushing the neighboring kingdom will be easy.

144
00:14:05,489 --> 00:14:08,180
And that neighboring kingdom will belong to you, Grand Duke.

145
00:14:08,505 --> 00:14:10,080
Splendid indeed.

146
00:14:12,449 --> 00:14:13,518
Sapphire is approaching!

147
00:14:13,542 --> 00:14:14,640
What?

148
00:14:14,840 --> 00:14:15,531
Hide it!

149
00:14:15,695 --> 00:14:16,842
Raise the curtain!

150
00:14:17,395 --> 00:14:19,231
Get the Grand Duke out of sight!

151
00:14:20,409 --> 00:14:21,409
We're ruined if we're found out!

152
00:14:21,570 --> 00:14:22,978
Quick, hide it!

153
00:14:39,559 --> 00:14:41,760
Move it! Move it!

154
00:14:49,200 --> 00:14:49,908
Hurry!

155
00:14:49,933 --> 00:14:50,500
Hurry!

156
00:14:53,319 --> 00:14:55,748
Someone stop it!

157
00:15:25,440 --> 00:15:26,440
Grand Duke Duralumin!

158
00:15:26,700 --> 00:15:27,922
What are you doing in a place like this?

159
00:15:28,065 --> 00:15:31,440
Ah, Prince Sapphire, we are merely investigating a rockslide.

160
00:15:37,150 --> 00:15:39,006
There isn't a sign of a rockslide anywhere!

161
00:15:39,420 --> 00:15:42,131
Duralumin, what on earth are you up to here?

162
00:15:42,795 --> 00:15:45,280
Oh no, Your Highness, I assure you we are doing nothing at all.

163
00:15:45,440 --> 00:15:46,440
Liar!

164
00:15:46,670 --> 00:15:49,520
Last night, I heard from Duke Blanc, the lord of this region,

165
00:15:49,544 --> 00:15:52,369
that you were planning to tear down Rose Mansion.

166
00:15:53,273 --> 00:15:54,480
Rose Mansion?

167
00:15:54,685 --> 00:15:55,685
Duke Blanc?

168
00:15:55,745 --> 00:15:57,144
I know nothing of this.

169
00:15:57,800 --> 00:15:58,800
Don't play dumb with me!

170
00:15:59,929 --> 00:16:02,486
Prince Sapphire, take a good look.

171
00:16:02,665 --> 00:16:05,940
Just where is this Rose Mansion supposed to be?

172
00:16:06,510 --> 00:16:09,220
There's no such thing in the Southern Valley.

173
00:16:10,440 --> 00:16:12,900
You must have been dreaming last night.

174
00:16:13,000 --> 00:16:13,504
How strange...

175
00:16:13,645 --> 00:16:14,820
Was it on top of the cliff, I wonder?

176
00:16:16,545 --> 00:16:18,620
That went well, Grand Duke.

177
00:16:23,520 --> 00:16:24,520
What is it?

178
00:16:24,870 --> 00:16:26,728
The me are working above.

179
00:16:26,752 --> 00:16:27,875
 You fool!

180
00:16:31,989 --> 00:16:33,291
What on earth are you doing?

181
00:16:34,380 --> 00:16:36,040
We are constructing a gun battery, Your Highness!

182
00:16:37,060 --> 00:16:38,060
A gun battery?

183
00:16:38,969 --> 00:16:42,640
That Duralumin... He intends to start a war with our neighbor on his own!

184
00:16:44,063 --> 00:16:45,095
All right, stop right there!

185
00:16:45,458 --> 00:16:48,288
I won't allow you to trample flowers just to prepare for war!

186
00:16:48,645 --> 00:16:49,480
Halt the construction!

187
00:16:49,665 --> 00:16:50,940
I won't let you do whatever you please!

188
00:16:50,964 --> 00:16:52,383
Do you care more about flowers than war?

189
00:16:52,408 --> 00:16:53,626
Tear this sham down!

190
00:17:16,060 --> 00:17:17,060
The rope!

191
00:17:22,773 --> 00:17:23,632
It's a fortress!

192
00:17:27,999 --> 00:17:28,999
Ouch!

193
00:17:59,029 --> 00:18:00,029
Have you come to?

194
00:18:01,469 --> 00:18:02,660
They are my friends.

195
00:18:02,844 --> 00:18:04,760
Grand Duke Duralumin did this to all of us.

196
00:18:06,129 --> 00:18:07,180
Grand Duke Duralumin?

197
00:18:10,379 --> 00:18:12,300
Ah! I can't believe they're just drenching people with water!

198
00:18:12,879 --> 00:18:14,900
Water is the greatest feast of all for us.

199
00:18:15,580 --> 00:18:15,900
What?

200
00:18:16,380 --> 00:18:17,440
Water is a feast?

201
00:18:28,899 --> 00:18:29,899
Pull yourself together!

202
00:18:30,649 --> 00:18:31,649
Stay strong!

203
00:18:36,909 --> 00:18:39,380
I see... was this all because of the flowers?

204
00:18:39,960 --> 00:18:40,360
That's right.

205
00:18:40,664 --> 00:18:42,540
It's all because of the flowers blooming in the Southern Valley.

206
00:18:43,084 --> 00:18:44,334
I am the Spirit of the White Rose,

207
00:18:44,358 --> 00:18:46,322
and my companions are the Spirits of the Weeds.

208
00:18:46,900 --> 00:18:49,337
Water is the finest feast for us. We took the form of humans

209
00:18:49,361 --> 00:18:51,400
and a mansion only because we wanted to speak with you.

210
00:18:52,124 --> 00:18:56,320
Every day, tens of thousands of our brethren are trampled by Grand Duke Duralumin.

211
00:18:57,014 --> 00:18:58,940
All for his ugly desire for war.

212
00:18:59,359 --> 00:19:00,940
So that's what you wanted to tell me.

213
00:19:01,844 --> 00:19:05,000
Duke Blanc, gather your friends! Let's defeat Grand Duke Duralumin!

214
00:19:07,919 --> 00:19:10,480
Sapphire, I must ask you not to meddle.

215
00:19:10,889 --> 00:19:12,800
What good comes from helping such wretched weeds?

216
00:19:13,020 --> 00:19:14,020
Rouge!

217
00:19:14,759 --> 00:19:17,256
We red roses shall move to Duralumin's estate

218
00:19:17,280 --> 00:19:19,300
and live peacefully in a sunny garden.

219
00:19:19,829 --> 00:19:21,996
Tended to every day by master gardeners.

220
00:19:22,021 --> 00:19:24,024
Do you care nothing for your brethren, Rouge?!

221
00:19:24,274 --> 00:19:26,760
I couldn't care less what happens to those filthy weeds!

222
00:19:27,020 --> 00:19:28,200
Traitor!

223
00:19:38,849 --> 00:19:40,557
Kumanbachi! Sting Sapphire!

224
00:20:14,834 --> 00:20:16,760
Master Sapphire, hurry, get on!

225
00:20:21,200 --> 00:20:21,940
I'm slipping.

226
00:20:22,200 --> 00:20:23,200
Hold on tight!

227
00:20:24,155 --> 00:20:26,380
You're no match for the Kumanbachi monster!

228
00:20:51,724 --> 00:20:52,677
It's the Kumanbachi!

229
00:21:01,821 --> 00:21:02,821
What a monster!

230
00:21:52,291 --> 00:21:53,661
Open up! Grand Duke Duralumin!

231
00:21:54,883 --> 00:21:55,352
Rouge!

232
00:21:56,939 --> 00:21:58,720
Why, Prince Sapphire!

233
00:21:59,079 --> 00:22:03,757
You see, this man has been saying something rather strange about you.

234
00:22:04,539 --> 00:22:10,740
He claims he will testify before everyone that you are actually a girl.

235
00:22:10,929 --> 00:22:14,460
Now, of course, it comes at a price. What are your terms?

236
00:22:14,969 --> 00:22:16,700
I do not have much longer to live.

237
00:22:16,984 --> 00:22:21,310
I want you to grow this in your garden, so that our kind may flourish once again.

238
00:22:21,334 --> 00:22:22,739
Plant this in my garden?

239
00:22:22,830 --> 00:22:24,940
Are you trying to make a fool out of Grand Duke Duralumin?

240
00:22:25,889 --> 00:22:30,340
I am Grand Duke Duralumin—cousin to the King of Silverland and Chief of Police!

241
00:22:30,594 --> 00:22:33,680
Do you really think such pitiful flowers would ever be planted in his garden?

242
00:22:46,934 --> 00:22:48,965
Our vital witness has vanished...

243
00:22:48,989 --> 00:22:49,863
Grand Duke Duralumin,

244
00:22:50,400 --> 00:22:52,026
about this fortress...

245
00:22:52,099 --> 00:22:53,753
Ah, Your Highness!

246
00:22:54,688 --> 00:22:57,900
The fortress was built because it was necessary to defend the kingdom.

247
00:22:57,925 --> 00:22:59,282
It was out of patriotism! —

248
00:22:59,306 --> 00:23:01,640
I shall speak to my father and obtain permission to tear it down.

249
00:23:02,114 --> 00:23:05,675
This Kingdom of Silverland has no need for patriotism that builds fortresses.

250
00:23:09,229 --> 00:23:10,600
It's Blanc! You're safe!

251
00:23:11,600 --> 00:23:13,920
Thank you. What happened to my brother?

252
00:23:18,729 --> 00:23:20,459
I see...

253
00:23:21,463 --> 00:23:22,960
Take heart, Duke Blanc.

254
00:23:23,599 --> 00:23:24,599
I'm going to demolish that fortress!

255
00:23:24,965 --> 00:23:28,620
Now your companions can live in the Southern Valley forever.

256
00:23:28,844 --> 00:23:30,560
Thank you, Prince Sapphire.

257
00:23:32,414 --> 00:23:36,340
The flowers and grass of the Southern Valley will never forget you.

258
00:23:38,480 --> 00:23:39,480
Farewell!

259
00:23:42,740 --> 00:23:45,295
Goodbye! So you were a spirit after all!

260
00:24:15,620 --> 00:24:19,240
♪ Tarari Ratta Ritta Ratta Rattattaa ♪
-

261
00:24:19,241 --> 00:24:22,601
♪ Kyahoo! Kyahoo! Kyahoo! ♪
Yahoo! Yahoo! Yahoo!

262
00:24:22,602 --> 00:24:26,372
♪ Tarari Ratta Ritta Ratta Rattattaa ♪
-

263
00:24:26,373 --> 00:24:29,534
♪ Kyahoo! Kyahoo! Kyahoo! ♪
Yahoo! Yahoo! Yahoo!

264
00:24:29,535 --> 00:24:33,348
♪ Sen'nen man'nen hyakuman-nen ♪
A thousand years, ten thousand years, a million years,

265
